Package: mysteryroster
Title: Registry Overlap Strata and Listing-Validity Analysis for Physician Directory Audits
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Tyler", "Muffly", email = "tyler.muffly@dhha.org", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2044-1693"))
Description: Tools for studies that test whether physician listings in national
    directories are valid. Cross-links any number of registries (for example NPPES,
    a certifying board, a professional society) by a common identifier into mutually
    exclusive overlap zones, draws a stratified listing sample that preserves sampling
    probabilities, turns telephone-audit dispositions into four exhaustive listing
    statuses (confirmed valid, confirmed invalid, unresolved, not attempted), and
    produces design-weighted validity estimates, extreme-case sensitivity bounds,
    survey-weighted regression, and study-flow counts. Specialty-agnostic: the ENT
    registry-validity study and the OB/GYN subspecialty study use the same functions
    with different registries and disposition codebooks.
